From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:08:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/20] venus: don't run a thread's TLS teardown from an
 unloaded driver

vn_tls_get() registers vn_tls_free as the destructor of a tss key the
first time a thread needs venus TLS state, which vkCreateDevice already
does. The destructor is in code that is unmapped the moment the last
vulkan instance is destroyed, which is not guaranteed to happen after
all threads that used venus have completed.

A thread that used venus and outlives its instance calls vn_tls_free
after it has been unmapped and crashes in glibc's __nptl_deallocate_tsd
when it exits. A thread that creates and destroys an instance and a
device and then returns is enough to hit it; so does a surfaceless EGL
context on zink over venus that is terminated before its thread exits.

To address this, delete the tss key from an atexit() handler, which
glibc runs when the driver is unloaded. Other threads still holding
venus TLS at that point leak it instead of calling into unmapped code.

Fixes: d17ddcc8477 ("venus: dispatch background shader tasks to secondary ring")
Cc: mesa-stable
Assisted-by: Claude Code
Signed-off-by: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44986>
(cherry picked from commit 935c4ec39a304de8f1078c4b6b1ebe1cbad9ce5e)
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c
index 84e3052faab..605631d26d0 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c
@@ -377,12 +377,31 @@ vn_tls_free(void *tls)
 static tss_t vn_tls_key;
 static bool vn_tls_key_valid;
 
+static void
+vn_tls_key_fini(void)
+{
+   vn_tls_key_valid = false;
+   vn_tls_free(tss_get(vn_tls_key));
+   tss_delete(vn_tls_key);
+}
+
 static void
 vn_tls_key_create_once(void)
 {
    vn_tls_key_valid = tss_create(&vn_tls_key, vn_tls_free) == thrd_success;
-   if (!vn_tls_key_valid && VN_DEBUG(INIT))
-      vn_log(NULL, "WARNING: failed to create vn_tls_key");
+   if (!vn_tls_key_valid) {
+      if (VN_DEBUG(INIT))
+         vn_log(NULL, "WARNING: failed to create vn_tls_key");
+      return;
+   }
+
+   /* Nothing ensures all threads that called vn_tls_get() have completed when
+    * the last vulkan instance is destroyed, which unmaps the driver.
+    *
+    * Delete the TLS key so that threads still holding venus TLS leak it
+    * instead of calling into unmapped code.
+    */
+   atexit(vn_tls_key_fini);
 }
 
 struct vn_tls *
